2:T73a,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a kitchen renovation near me cost in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, a professional kitchen renovation may typically cost around £10,000–£35,000, but a cosmetic refresh can cost less and a redesigned or structurally altered kitchen can cost considerably more. Every project differs, so request a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is usually included in a kitchen renovation quote?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It may include cabinets, worktops, fitting and some services, but plumbing, electrics, appliances, tiling, flooring, waste removal, VAT and decorating can vary. Check every item and exclusion in writing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many kitchen renovation quotes should I get?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Getting two or three detailed quotes can be a practical comparison. Give each company the same brief and compare the specification, exclusions, allowances, programme and payment terms rather than just the total."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to keep the existing kitchen layout?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often, yes. Retaining the positions of plumbing, waste, gas and electrical points can reduce labour and materials, although the existing services still need to be assessed for condition and suitability."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a local renovation company handle all the kitchen trades?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Some companies coordinate or handle several trades, while others use separate subcontractors. Ask who is responsible for plumbing, electrics, tiling, cabinet installation and finishing work before accepting a quote."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-renovation-near-me-cost","d"]
